-- title:
--   Algebraisation over ℚ̄ of a lifted endomorphism
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a valuation subring $A_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $\kappa_0 = \mathrm{ResidueField}(A_0)$ has characteristic $p$, a Weierstrass curve $W$ over $\kappa_0$, and an arbitrary self-map $\beta_0$ of the set of affine points of $W$ (no additivity is assumed). Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $0$, $B$ a valuation subring of $L$ with residue field $\kappa_B$, $\varphi \colon \kappa_0 \xrightarrow{\sim} \kappa_B$ a ring isomorphism, and $E'$ a Weierstrass curve over $B$ whose discriminant is a unit and whose reduction $E' \bmod \mathfrak{m}_B$ has nonzero discriminant $\Delta$; assume the $j$-invariant of $E'$ viewed over $L$ is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, and that a variable change $v'$ over $\kappa_B$ satisfies $v' \cdot (E' \bmod \mathfrak{m}_B) = W_{\varphi}$, where $W_\varphi$ denotes $W$ with coefficients pushed along $\varphi$. Let $\beta'$ be an additive self-map of the affine points of $E'$ over $L$ lying in `rationalHomSet`, i.e. either zero or given, outside a finite set of $x$-coordinates, by a quotient of bivariate polynomials over $L$ in each coordinate. Assume the compatibility: for every point $Q$ of $E'$ over $L$ and every point $P_0$ of $W$, if $\varphi$ applied coordinatewise to $P_0$ equals the image of the reduction of $Q$ under the inverse of the point bijection attached to $v'$, then the same relation holds with $P_0$, $Q$ replaced by $\beta_0 P_0$, $\beta' Q$. Then there exist a valuation subring $A'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a ring isomorphism $e \colon \mathrm{ResidueField}(A') \xrightarrow{\sim} \kappa_0$, a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $A'$ whose reduction modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{A'}$ has nonzero discriminant, a variable change $v$ over $\kappa_0$ with $v \cdot ((E \bmod \mathfrak{m}_{A'})_e) = W$, and an additive self-map $\alpha$ of the affine points of $E$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in `rationalHomSet`, such that for every such point $P$, transporting the reduction of $\alpha P$ along $e$ and the bijection attached to $v$ gives exactly $\beta_0$ applied to the corresponding transport of the reduction of $P$.
--
--   This is the algebraisation and descent step in Deuring's lifting theorem: a good model with an endomorphism, produced over an arbitrary algebraically closed valued field of characteristic $0$ but with algebraic $j$-invariant, is realised over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at some place above $p$, with the prescribed reduction data and the prescribed action $\beta_0$ on the special fibre. The place $A'$ and the residue identification $e$ are not prescribed here; the result feeds the lifting statement [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_variableChange_smul_eq_and_reduceHom_comp_eq_comp_reduceHom_of_comp_self_add_smul_eq_smul`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_variableChange_smul_eq_and_reduceHom_comp_eq_comp_reduceHom_of_comp_self_add_smul_eq_smul).
